# Runtime-written local files that must NEVER ship in a deploy image — these
# are gitignored (see .gitignore) but .dockerignore is a SEPARATE list, so
# `COPY . .` in the Dockerfile was baking whatever stale local copy existed
# on the deploying machine into every image, silently resetting live
# production data back to that snapshot on every single deploy. Caught via
# insights/data/generated-insights.json specifically (see project memory) —
# excluding the whole data/ pattern here so no future local-only file repeats it.
insights/data/
